data: {"text":"1. That my client had sold a used Mahindra Thar vehicle bearing registration number JH-01-AB-"}

data: {"text":"1234 to you vide sale agreement dated 01.02.2026, and there remained"}

data: {"text":" a balance amount of Rs. 2,25,000/- (Rupees Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) towards the sale consideration payable by you to my client as"}

data: {"text":" per the terms of the said sale agreement.\n\n2. That towards discharge of the aforesaid liability, you issued Cheque No. 672145 dated"}

data: {"text":" 10.04.2026 for Rs. 2,25,000/- (Rupees Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) drawn on State Bank of India, Main Branch, Ranchi, in favour"}

data: {"text":" of my client.\n\n3. That the said cheque was duly presented for collection to the payee's bank on 15.04.2026 through"}

data: {"text":" proper banking channels, but the same was returned dishonoured vide bank's return memo dated 17.04.2026 with the endorsement \""}

data: {"text":"Account Closed\".\n\n4. That the dishonour of the said cheque constitutes a criminal offence under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, which"}

