event: template_sections
data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 138 read with Section 142 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881)\n\nDate: 06 May 2026\nBy Registered Post A.D. / Speed Post / UPC\n\nTo,\nMr. Dilip Kumar Singh\nHouse No. 102, Bariatu, Ranchi - 834009\n\nFrom,\nMr. Sanjay Prasad\nThrough: Adv. Neelam Kumari, Advocate\nChamber 21, District Court Compound, Ranchi - 834001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Statutory Demand Notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 — Cheque No. 672145 dated 10.04.2026 for Rs. 225000/- (Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) drawn on State Bank of India, Main Branch, Ranchi — dishonoured on 17.04.2026\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, Mr. Sanjay Prasad, I hereby serve upon you this statutory notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, and call upon you to note as under:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That my client had sold a used Mahindra Thar vehicle bearing registration number JH-01-AB-1234 to you vide sale agreement dated 01.02.2026, and there remained a balance amount of Rs. 2,25,000/- (Rupees Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) towards the sale consideration payable by you to my client as per the terms of the said sale agreement.\n\n2. That towards discharge of the aforesaid liability, you issued Cheque No. 672145 dated 10.04.2026 for Rs. 2,25,000/- (Rupees Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) drawn on State Bank of India, Main Branch, Ranchi, in favour of my client.\n\n3. That the said cheque was duly presented for collection to the payee's bank on 15.04.2026 through proper banking channels, but the same was returned dishonoured vide bank's return memo dated 17.04.2026 with the endorsement \"Account Closed\".\n\n4. That the dishonour of the said cheque constitutes a criminal offence under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, which is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.\n\n5. That as per the proviso (b) to Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, the payee is required to make a demand for payment of the said amount of cheque within thirty days of receiving information of the dishonour of the cheque by the drawee bank.\n\n6. That my client received the information regarding dishonour of the aforesaid cheque on 18.04.2026 and this legal notice is being served upon you well within the statutory period of thirty days from the date of receipt of such information."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to make payment of the said sum of Rs. 225000/- (Two Lakh Twenty Five Thousand only) to my client within a period of fifteen (15) days from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate criminal proceedings against you under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, before the competent Magistrate having jurisdiction, at your risk, cost, and consequences.\n\nPlease note that under Section 138, if you fail to make payment within 15 days of receipt of this notice, my client shall file a criminal complaint within 30 days thereafter, and upon conviction you shall be liable to imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further legal action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Neelam Kumari\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. JHC/1893/2019\nChamber 21, District Court Compound, Ranchi - 834001\n\n(Counsel for Mr. Sanjay Prasad)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

